# /i/HOUSE7 is a path, not a file. One page reads the code out of the URL, so there is
# nothing to generate per event and nothing to rebuild when an event is created.
#
# 200, not 301: a redirect would change the URL in the address bar and, more importantly,
# Apple's universal-link matching runs against the URL as SENT. Rewriting keeps /i/CODE.
# THE DESTINATION IS `/i/`, NOT `/i/index.html`. Pages canonicalises the explicit filename
# -- `/i/index.html` answers 308 to `/i/` -- and a rewrite whose target redirects does not
# serve, so `/i/SR1017` 404'd on the first deploy with the file spelled out. Measured, not
# guessed: `/i/` returns 200 text/html and `/i/index.html` returns 308.
/i/*  /i/  200
